  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nHigh pressure will linger across the Quad State through Friday \nmorning, bringing a break in the heat and humidity as well as the \nprecipitation. \n\nThe next chance of precipitation (30-50$) will arrive Friday into \nSaturday as a shortwave and deeper moisture approaches from the \nPlains. Precipitable water values are still forecast to jump up to \naround 2 inches, which again, supports very heavy downpours. The \nshortwave will then push east of the area Saturday morning, which \nwill allow for mainly dry conditions for the rest of the weekend.\n\nUpper-level riding will build into the Quad State over the weekend \nand for at least the first half of next week, bringing hot \ntemperatures (in the mid 90s) and increased humidity (dewpoints \nclimbing into the 70s.) The combination of the two, will lead to \nheat index values pushing back up into the 100-105 degree range with \nonly limited chances for afternoon thunderstorms.",
